 building small  services as well as  large enterprise applications now we  will move ahead and  understand tips to learn python at a  bare minimum  you and your resource must cover the  fundamentals  without understanding them you will have  a hard time working through complex  problems  projects or use cases examples of  python's fundamentals include  variables and types lists dictionaries  and sets basic operators string  formatting  basic string operations conditions  loops functions list comprehensions  classes and objects after covering all  the fundamentals  you should establish a goal for your  study  before you start learning python  establish a goal  for your study you will know what  learning material to focus on  or skim through as it pertains to your  goals  for example if you are interested in  becoming a machine learning  engineer you should refer to only that  relevant  material there are several tech  industries that use  python for development machine learning  and ai  web development game development and  internet of things once you have  established your goal  you should also have a look at relevant  python libraries that helps you reach  your goal  there are hundreds of libraries that are  used by python developers  and different domains these libraries  make your life easier  since they reduce manual workload and  wrap code for specialized tasks  these libraries make your life easier  since they reduce  manual workload and wrap up the code for  specialized works  there are many popular libraries out  there for example  django for web development pandas for  data analysis  and many more some of the most popular  python libraries  are tensorflow for machine learning  flask  for web development scrapy for web  scraping  buy game for game development after  doing all this  now you are ready to make and work on  python projects  on your own it is very important to  apply  what you learn while learning each  python concept  making projects as you progress is  highly recommended  since it will make you a good coder and  expand your portfolio  don't expect to make industry standard  projects from the start  but improve upon them as you learn more  some of the interesting ideas that you  can base your projects on  are number guessing web scraper  calculator searching and sorting  tic-tac-toe game  consistency is really important no  matter what you learn  or do it is not realistic for anyone to  expect to become a developer within a  week  except be consistent and work towards  short-term goals and reach those goals  within a set time frame remember  two hours daily for a month are always  going to be more productive  than cramming everything within a week's  time  now moving ahead let's have a look at  python industry trends and  ultimately add the scope of a python  developer  in the last several years python has  seen enormous growth in demand  with no sign of slowing down the  programming language her ranking site  pypl has ranked python as the number one  programming language  with a considerable popularity gain in  the year 2019  as well as in the year 2020.  also python has surpassed java and  become the second most popular language  according to github repositories  contributions  machine learning is probably the most  popular field  in the tech industry right now python  because of its variety of libraries and  the preferred language  for performing machine learning tasks  libraries like numpy pandas tensorflow  are  widely used in machine learning and  artificial intelligence  so if you are into machine learning and  artificial intelligence  python should be the right language for  you  software engineers with python skills  are offered better salaries across the  globe  average python developer salary in india  is  7 lakhs 55 497  per annum average python developer  salary in the united states of america  is 79 395  american dollars there you go we hope  you are now motivated enough to start  your learning journey  and are ready to keep working on getting  better at bison  we also have a python youtube playlist  that covers everything  from very basics to advanced python  concepts  the link is added in the description and  with that  we have reached to the end of this video  hope you liked it  think we miss anything important let us  know in the live chat  or in the comment sections below if  you're watching this later  thank you for  you

